er-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f8df05a-8103-54f3-a620-1e133a56c17a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673085} :answer-field/id #uuid "2dd00408-b9a0-5f12-9fa0-541b03b0b6a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673067}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "20ccd7a5-e8b5-55f6-85dc-37a089ac87ea" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices have a rank of $3?$\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 & 4 & 0 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 8 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 2 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & -6\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$C=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that a matrix of rank $3$ must have at least $3$ columns and at least $3$ rows. \nSo, we disregard the matrix $B$ since it has only $2$ rows. \n\nAlso, the matrix must have $3$ pivot columns. As we can see, the matrix $A$ has exactly $3$ pivot columns. So, $\\text{rank}(A)=3.$ As we can see, the matrix $C$ has only $2$ pivot columns. So, $\\text{rank}(C)=2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$A$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673066 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31ae6bd4-af46-5895-b8d2-1af2b3ab22a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673071} {:answer/id #uuid "8a9873b5-a61d-54e1-ae43-bf4dc7e8508c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ and $B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673083} {:answer/id #uuid "a4069f21-8bd8-5ab1-a95f-d93b37df1684" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 175921860454